mailove (2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed from Mailo to Mailove. The binary, the desktop entry, the icon
    and the internal URL scheme all follow the new name.
  * Because the application name changed, settings and cached mail now live
    under ~/.config/mailove/ and ~/.local/share/mailove/. Nothing is migrated
    from the old mailo directories: accounts must be added again and each
    one re-syncs from the server on first use. The old directories are left
    untouched and can be removed by hand.

 -- Daniel Duris <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Better spam identification.
  * UI and UX fixes against the 20 ms rule: message pages are prefetched
    ahead of the scroll, and holding Page Down no longer degrades over a
    long list.
  * Read-only folders now fail cleanly instead of surfacing a rejected
    STORE.
  * Background workers run at low priority, so they no longer compete with
    the GUI thread.
  * Logging changed: switched off now means a silent console.
  * Added a GUI-thread stall detector and paging timings for diagnostics,
    both reported only when logging is enabled.
  * Groundwork for Gravatar sender icons is present but inert: not built,
    not reachable from the UI, and likely to be removed — an avatar lookup
    tells a third party who is mailing you, which is not a switch worth
    offering even off by default.

 -- Daniel Duris <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 21:24:40 +0200

mailove (2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Accounts other than the open one now sync their mail in the background,
    not just their unread counts. Each refresh walks that account's folders —
    the inbox first, the rest after — and caches everything that arrived since
    the last visit, so switching to an account shows the mail its unread badge
    already promised instead of fetching it then.
  * Packaging: the .deb and the AppImage are both written to the project root,
    named with the version, and CPack's staging directory is cleaned up after
    itself. `cmake --build build --target packages` builds both.
  * The AppImage build no longer requires FUSE on the build machine; where the
    kernel device is missing the packaging tools run in extract-and-run mode.

 -- Daniel Duris <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * JMAP support (RFC 8620/8621). An account now chooses its protocol: IMAP
    as before, or JMAP, which discovers its own endpoints from the address
    and authenticates with an API token or a password. Both kinds of account
    can be configured at once.
  * Mail protocols sit behind one interface, so which mailbox is the trash,
    when to backfill and what a header means are answered the same way
    whichever protocol replied. Push arrives as IMAP IDLE or JMAP
    EventSource and is handled identically.
  * Fixed: migrating an account from a pre-1.0 install silently reset its
    IMAP port to 993, its security to SSL/TLS and lost its SMTP settings.
    The values were read from the wrong settings scope.
  * Fixed: after the wallet lookup finished, a connection requested while it
    was still in flight was never resumed, so the client could sit offline
    with a perfectly good account configured.
  * Fixed: a DKIM or OpenPGP verdict on a message rebuilt from the cache
    could be attributed to whichever message was on screen when a delayed
    retry landed, reporting cache staleness as tampering.
  * Quieter status bar: breadcrumbs that only repeated what the window
    already showed (an empty folder, a link opening in the browser) are gone
    from the status line and kept in the debug log.
  * Internals: the mail controller is split into an account store, a sync
    engine, a cache-maintenance scheduler, a message presenter and a
    signature verifier, each testable on its own. The test suite grew to
    twelve binaries covering the cache, account storage and the attachment
    split/restore pair.

 -- Daniel Duris <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Unread counts in the folder pane: a pill on every folder, blue on the
    inbox, and an outline on a collapsed folder standing in for the unread
    sitting in subfolders folded away beneath it.
  * Other accounts are checked for new mail on the refresh schedule — connect,
    STATUS, disconnect — so their unread counts move without switching to them.
  * Spam retention (Settings, General): mail sent longer ago than the chosen
    number of days is removed from the spam folder automatically, going by the
    date the message carries. "Skip trash for spam" (on by default) deletes it
    outright rather than filing it in the trash to be cleared out twice.
  * Folders can be dragged onto another folder to reparent them, or onto the
    account name to move them to the top level. Imported archives included.
  * Rename folder in the folder context menu. Where the protocol forbids it —
    INBOX, and the special-use mailboxes a server recreates — the menu says so
    in place of the command.
  * Message context menu, starting with Mark unread. A message marked unread
    while open stays open and stays unread; it is marked read again the next
    time it is opened.
  * A "No label" key that clears any colour label, alongside the five.
  * Junk is called spam throughout the interface, except where a folder is
    named otherwise by the server.
  * Fixes: an account switch no longer carries the previous account's folder
    delimiter, which could rewrite an imported archive's folder paths; folder
    trees keep parents directly above their children; folders in the sidebar
    could not be dragged at all.

 -- Daniel Duris <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Tue, 04 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Compose, Settings and opened messages are tabs in the main window rather
    than separate windows; the composer can still be a window of its own
    (Settings, Look and feel).
  * Accounts keep the e-mail address they send from separately from the login
    name, so the two may differ, and can carry a full name and organization.
  * Imported mail is its own account type, without server settings.
  * Accounts can be reordered by dragging them in the folder pane.
  * Message list: Page Up/Down, Home/End, Enter to open, Ctrl+W to close a
    tab, and the keyboard follows the folder you open.
  * Much faster paging through large folders, and background updates no
    longer slow down as more of a folder is loaded.
  * Reclaiming disk space no longer freezes the window while it starts.
  * File pickers are the desktop's own, with its colours and Places sidebar.

 -- Daniel Duris <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Attachments are stored as content-addressed files outside the database,
    deduplicated and zstd-compressed; existing caches are migrated in place.
  * Cache maintenance in Settings: reported size, and an explicit vacuum to
    return free space to the filesystem.
  * Gmail's All Mail archive is excluded from caching and hidden, removing
    the duplicate copy of every message.
  * Compose: Save as draft, resuming a draft from the Drafts folder, and a
    confirmation before a message is discarded.
  * Shortcuts act anywhere in the window rather than only in the message list.
  * Settings dialog is resizable and remembers its size.
  * Faster start-up, and folder and message selection no longer lost to
    background refreshes.

 -- Daniel Duris <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200

